{
 "note": "Transition (Harrie Fasher, 2016; Rio Tinto Sculpture Award, Sculpture by the Sea Cottesloe 2018, gifted to the City in Aug 2018), on the foreshore lawn west of the playground, from the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026), OSM and photos. A horse rising out of the ground, about 6 m long and 4 m high, made as an open frame of rusted steel flat bar with a few plates: haunches on the ground, the body and arched neck rearing up, the head bowed forward, one foreleg bent and the other reaching flat along the grass. Bollards and a wire round it. Approximated as stepped bars and thin plates; the real one wants a Blender layer. Metres: x along the horse from its haunch to its hoof (bearing 165), y across its body.",
